    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present No. 4, a spacious and beautifully presented two-bedroom duplex apartment, set within an exclusive development of just 12 homes in the heart of Naul Village.\n\nThis captivating development occupies a picturesque setting amid landscaped communal gardens on the banks of the Delvin River. Rich in character and history, the building incorporates the original limestone façade of a former miller's house, dating back to the early 1740s, creating a wonderful sense of old-world charm.\n\nExtending to approximately 86 sq. m, No. 4 is presented in turnkey condition. The accommodation is bright, spacious and thoughtfully arranged over two levels. At entrance level, the welcoming hallway includes valuable understairs storage and a guest WC. The living room features a charming Juliet balcony, while the separate kitchen provides an excellent space for everyday living. Upstairs are two spacious double bedrooms, with the main bedroom benefiting from a second Juliet balcony. A generously appointed main bathroom, complete with a Jacuzzi bath and separate shower, completes the accommodation. The property also benefits from attic storage.\n\nThe development enjoys beautifully maintained communal grounds and open green space overlooking the Delvin River, while a pedestrian entrance provides quick and convenient access to the village's Main Street. Shops, services and local amenities are all within easy reach.\n\nNaul is a charming and welcoming village offering an appealing balance of countryside living and excellent accessibility. Dublin Airport, the M1 and M50 motorways, Dublin City Centre and the surrounding towns of Balbriggan, Skerries and Swords are all within convenient driving distance.\n\nNo. 4 offers a rare opportunity to acquire a spacious, turnkey home in a unique historic setting and will appeal equally to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Superbly restored former 17th-century miller's house</li><li> Original limestone façade dating to the early 1740s</li><li> Landscaped communal gardens</li><li> Beautiful open green space overlooking the Delvin River</li><li> Recessed lighting</li><li> Gas-fired central heating</li><li> Double-glazed Rationel windows throughout</li><li> Two feature Juliet balconies, serving the living room and main bedroom</li><li> Two generous double bedrooms</li><li> Main bathroom with Jacuzzi bath and separate shower</li><li> Guest WC</li><li> Annual management fee of approximately 2,400</li><li> Managed by Curran Property Management</ul>"
      },
